= Symbols, arrows, and fallback

Common math: $ forall x in RR: x^2 >= 0 quad exists y in RR: y^2 = 2 $

Arrows and sets: $ A union B subset.eq C arrow.r A inter B $

Less common Unicode characters as text: ⇫ ⇬ ⇭ ⇮ ⇯ ⇰ ⇱ ⇲ ⇳.

The same arrows in math: $ ⇫ ⇬ ⇭ ⇮ ⇯ ⇰ ⇱ ⇲ ⇳ $.

The examples above intentionally include characters with different cmap coverage.
